## 6. Guardrails

### Online (Real-Time)

These run inside `ai_service.generate_text` via `guardrail_service.scan_and_log` on every
call. Phase 13 adds no new online guardrails — the existing infrastructure covers the
critical paths.

| Guardrail | What It Catches | Intervention | Where It Lives |
|-----------|----------------|--------------|----------------|
| **Injection scan (input)** | Control names containing adversarial instruction patterns (e.g., "ignore previous instructions", XML tag injection via `<>{}`) | `generate_text` returns `BLOCKED:` string; `compliance_narrative_service` catches it and returns static fallback. PDF delivery proceeds. | `guardrail_service.scan_and_log` inside `ai_service.generate_text` — already wired |
| **PII scan (output)** | Narrative output containing tenant PII that should not appear in a PDF report section (email addresses, IP addresses, API keys in control descriptions) | Same as above — `BLOCKED:` triggers fallback | `guardrail_service.scan_and_log` on the output string — already wired |
| **Word budget check (output)** | Narrative exceeding word limit before PDF injection | `_trim_to_words(result, limit)` in `compliance_narrative_service` — hard truncation, no fallback needed | Post-processing in `generate_executive_summary` / `generate_framework_narrative` |
| **Error-string prefix check** | `generate_text` returning `"BLOCKED:"` or `"Error:"` instead of a narrative | Static fallback template returned; `_build_pdf` receives a valid string | `result.startswith(("BLOCKED:", "Error:"))` guard in `compliance_narrative_service` |

**Latency note:** The existing `scan_and_log` guardrail adds ~10–30 ms per call. This is
acceptable for a background report scheduler with no synchronous user waiting.

**Gap — cross-tenant isolation:** There is no online guardrail that detects cross-tenant
data leakage at the narrative layer. This is mitigated architecturally: `_generate_report`
is called with a single tenant's data, and `compliance_narrative_service` is stateless.
The prompt never contains data from more than one tenant. Monitor via Phoenix span
attributes (Section 7).

---

### Offline (Flywheel)

These run as sampled batch analysis feeding the prompt improvement loop. They are not
blocking — a failure here triggers a ticket, not a report block.

| Metric | Sampling Strategy | Measurement | Action on Degradation |
|--------|------------------|-------------|----------------------|
| **Control-to-narrative fidelity rate** | 100% of narratives sampled for the first 30 days post-GA; then 25% random sample ongoing | LLM Judge (D1 rubric) | If fidelity rate drops below 90% in any 7-day window: review prompt, add few-shot examples, re-run reference dataset |
| **Severity framing accuracy rate** | 25% random sample; 100% for multi-framework reports | LLM Judge (D3 rubric) | If accuracy drops below 85%: investigate whether severity fields are being passed correctly from `scheduled_reports_service`; consider adding severity ordering to the prompt explicitly |
| **Remediation specificity score** | 10% random sample + all narratives for tenants with Critical-severity failing controls | LLM Judge (D4 5-point rubric) | If mean score drops below 3.0: add a concrete remediation few-shot example to the system instruction |
| **Fallback rate** | 100% (logged by `compliance_narrative_service` at WARNING level) | Code (count of WARNING log entries with `[NarrativeService] generate_text failed`) | If fallback rate exceeds 5% over any 24h window: check circuit breaker state, Anthropic API status, and `ai_breaker` open/closed logs |
| **Word budget compliance rate** | 100% (code check, near-zero cost) | Code (`len(text.split()) <= limit` before `_trim_to_words`) | If raw output exceeds word limit on >20% of calls: tighten the word-count instruction or reduce `max_tokens` on the provider |
| **Scope containment pass rate** | 25% random sample | LLM Judge (D2 rubric — checks for temporal fabrication) | If rate drops below 95%: add explicit constraint to system prompt: "Do not reference prior periods or future trajectory unless the data block contains a `prior_period` field." |

**Flywheel cadence:** Batch runs weekly via a scheduled Celery task. LLM Judge calls use
`claude-haiku-3-5` (not Sonnet) to keep flywheel cost under $2/month. Results written to
`ai_narrative_eval_results` MongoDB collection per tenant, per week.

