## 7. Production Monitoring

**Tracing Tool:** Arize Phoenix (already wired in `app_startup.py` via
`AnthropicInstrumentor().instrument()`). Access at `http://localhost:6006`.
Phoenix must be self-hosted within the tenant VPC — do not route compliance narrative
content to a cloud Phoenix SaaS instance (same constraint as Phase 12's T-12-07 note).

**Span filter for Phase 13:** Filter by `source` attribute in Phoenix:
- `compliance_narrative` — executive summary spans
- `compliance_narrative_framework` — per-framework narrative spans

---

### Key Metrics to Track

| Metric | Source | Description |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| `ai_narrative_latency_ms` | Phoenix span duration | P50/P95 latency per `generate_text` call for narrative generation. Budget: P95 ≤ 5000 ms |
| `ai_narrative_tokens_used` | Phoenix span token attributes | Input + output tokens per call. Budget: ≤ 600 tokens per call (Section 4b.5) |
| `ai_narrative_fallback_rate` | Application logs (`[NarrativeService] generate_text failed`) | Percentage of calls returning static fallback. Baseline: < 2% |
| `ai_narrative_word_budget_exceeded` | Application logs (WARNING when raw output exceeds limit) | Count of calls where the model ignored the word-limit instruction. Baseline: < 10% |
| `ai_breaker_state` | Circuit breaker logs (`[AI] Circuit breaker open`) | Open/closed state of `ai_breaker`; an open circuit means all narrative calls are falling back |

---

### Alert Thresholds

| Condition | Severity | Response |
|-----------|----------|----------|
| Fallback rate > 5% over any 30-minute window | Warning | Investigate Anthropic API status and `ai_breaker` state; check `scheduled_reports_service` logs for downstream PDF delivery failures |
| Fallback rate > 20% over any 60-minute window | Critical | Page on-call; check for Anthropic API outage; verify circuit breaker is not stuck open |
| P95 narrative latency > 8000 ms | Warning | Review token counts; check for prompt expansion (abnormally long control names); consider reducing `failing_controls` slice from 7 to 5 |
| Any narrative span with `source=compliance_narrative` containing a tenant ID in the Phoenix span attributes that does not match the expected tenant for the report run | Critical | Potential cross-tenant data leak — halt narrative generation, audit `_generate_report` call stack for the affected run |
| `ai_breaker` state transitions to OPEN during business hours | Warning | Alert compliance team that reports scheduled in the next window will use static fallback templates |

---

### Smart Sampling Strategy

Weight human review toward interactions most likely to surface domain failures — not random
sampling.

| Signal | Sample Rate | Reviewer |
|--------|------------|----------|
| Narrative for a tenant with compliance score 50–65% (borderline — highest audit risk) | 100% for the first 60 days post-GA; then 50% | GRC Analyst |
| Narrative for a multi-framework report (SOC 2 + ISO 27001 simultaneously) | 50% | GRC Analyst — framework conflation most likely here |
| Any narrative that triggered `_trim_to_words` truncation (raw output exceeded word limit) | 100% | Engineer — verify truncation did not cut a critical control name |
| Any narrative returned via static fallback | 100% | Engineer — root cause why `generate_text` failed for this report run |
| Quarterly random sample for CISO readability review | 5–10 executive summaries per quarter | CISO or VP of Security |
| Narratives where the LLM Judge flagged fidelity score < 3 in the offline flywheel | 100% of flagged | GRC Analyst — human arbitration before any prompt change |

**Review SLA:** GRC Analyst reviews must complete within 5 business days of the report
delivery date — audit packages are typically assembled within 2 weeks of the report date.
Findings from human review feed back into the reference dataset expansion and LLM Judge
rubric calibration.

